# P09.31 — v1 coverage bundle: empty-class size, class field
# attributes, class-header generics, plus validation probes for
# non-trivial virtual signatures and multi-field Swift class
# bindings.
#
# Five queue items folded into one patch because each is small
# and they're thematically related ("v1 polish / coverage").
#
# - **#5 empty polymorphic class size**: Clang emits 8 bytes for
#   `struct Widget { virtual foo(); };`; we emitted 16 due to
#   `#[repr(cpp)]`'s empty-class size=1 rule composing with the
#   P09.25 vptr shift. Fix in `cxx_bridge::correct_layout`:
#   collapse the empty-bump before the shift when the user
#   declared no fields. Result: vptr-only polymorphic classes
#   are now 8 bytes.
# - **#6 class field attributes**: P09.30 routed any
#   `#`-prefixed member in a `class` body to the method path,
#   so users couldn't attach `#[doc]` / `#[cfg]` / `#[serde]` to
#   fields. Added a bounded token-scan helper
#   `skip_over_outer_attributes` and dispatched on the token
#   that follows the attr group. Fields now carry attributes
#   just like struct fields do.
# - **#7 generics on class header**: `pub class Pair<A, B> { … }`
#   already parsed (via `parse_generics`), but the synthesized
#   inherent impl wrote `impl<A, B> Pair { … }` with the
#   self-type path missing the `<A, B>` arguments. Added
#   `build_cxx_class_self_path` that emits a path segment
#   with `AngleBracketedArgs` referencing each of the class's
#   params (lifetimes → `GenericArg::Lifetime`, type params →
#   `GenericArg::Type(Path(ident))`, const params → same
#   Type-shape fallback; real const generics aren't v1).
#   Also: `itanium::is_cpp_abi` now skips C++ mangling when
#   the impl or fn has any non-synthetic generic params
#   (Itanium can't express them, and per-monomorphization
#   symbols would collide under a single NO_MANGLE).
#   `codegen_attrs` NO_MANGLE path gains the same guard.
# - **#1 non-trivial virtual signatures**: validated via
#   `/tmp/p09-35-virtsigs/`. Virtuals with multi-arg primitive
#   signatures, `&Point` refs to another cpp class, and
#   `*const Point` pointers all mangle and dispatch correctly.
#   No code changes needed.
# - **#9 multi-field Swift class-backed bindings**: validated
#   via `/tmp/p09-33-swift-multi/`. The existing
#   `memcpy + overwrite-ptr-at-0` Clone logic already handles
#   POD extra fields (e.g. a `tag: u64` alongside the class
#   handle). No code changes needed. Non-POD extra fields
#   (another class handle) remain a documented limitation.
#
# # Validation
#
# - `/tmp/p09-small-poly/` — Tiny polymorphic class, now
#   `sret([8 x i8])` instead of 16. `kind() = 42, exit 0`.
# - `/tmp/p09-30-class-kw/` — field attrs version passes.
#   `foo() = 109, bar() = 18 — OK`.
# - `/tmp/p09-34-class-generics/` — generic `class Pair<A, B>`
#   builds clean; `demo() = 1`.
# - `/tmp/p09-35-virtsigs/` — mixed virtual signatures.
#   `scaled=52 encloses=1 area_plus_point=17 — OK`.
# - `/tmp/p09-33-swift-multi/` — multi-field class binding.
#   All four deinit-count checkpoints match expectations,
#   tag preserved through Clone.
# - `cargo test --workspace` → 235/0 preserved.
#
# # Files
#
# - `compiler/rustc_ty_utils/src/layout/cxx_bridge.rs` — empty-
#   class collapse.
# - `compiler/rustc_parse/src/parser/item.rs` — skip-attrs
#   helper, field/method dispatch, generic self-path builder.
# - `compiler/rustc_symbol_mangling/src/itanium.rs` — generic
#   methods skip C++ mangling.
# - `compiler/rustc_codegen_ssa/src/codegen_attrs.rs` — same
#   guard on the NO_MANGLE auto-export path.
#
# No workspace changes.
